<% content_for :title, "State persistence — shadcnrb" %>

<div class="space-y-8">
  <div class="space-y-2">
    <%= sui.h1 "State persistence" %>
    <%= sui.lead do %>
      Two components remember a choice across requests: the theme switcher
      (theme and light/dark mode) and the sidebar (expanded or collapsed).
      Both persist in a cookie by default and render server-side, so nothing
      flashes on load. Both can persist on your backend instead, with the
      cookie as the fallback.
    <% end %>
  </div>

  <%= sui.separator %>

  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%= sui.h2 "How it works" %>
    <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 text-sm leading-relaxed">
      <li><strong>Read side</strong> — a helper renders the state into the HTML. It takes the value as an argument and falls back to the cookie when the argument is <%= sui.code "nil" %>. Precedence: argument, then cookie, then default.</li>
      <li><strong>Write side</strong> — the component always writes its cookie, then dispatches a Stimulus <%= sui.code "change" %> event with the new value. The gem never issues a request; your app listens if it wants to store the value.</li>
      <li><strong>Failure</strong> — if your request fails, the cookie keeps the page correct until the next server render, where your stored value wins.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>

  <%= sui.separator %>

  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%= sui.h2 "Theme and mode" %>
    <%= sui.p "Cookie (default). Put the helper on <html>; the switcher writes the shadcnrb_theme and shadcnrb_mode cookies:", class: "text-sm" %>
<pre class="rounded-md bg-muted px-4 py-3 overflow-x-auto text-xs font-mono"><code>&lt;html class="&lt;%= sui.theme_class %&gt;"&gt;
  …
  &lt;%= sui.theme_switcher %&gt;</code></pre>

    <%= sui.p "Backend. Pass the stored values; the event detail is always { theme, mode }, whichever one changed:", class: "text-sm" %>
<pre class="rounded-md bg-muted px-4 py-3 overflow-x-auto text-xs font-mono"><code>&lt;html class="&lt;%= sui.theme_class(theme: current_user.theme, mode: current_user.mode) %&gt;"&gt;

shadcnrb--theme-switcher--component:change   detail: { theme: "blue", mode: "dark" }</code></pre>
  </div>

  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%= sui.h2 "Sidebar" %>
    <%= sui.p "Cookie (default). The wrapper reads the sidebar_state cookie, which a desktop toggle writes:", class: "text-sm" %>
<pre class="rounded-md bg-muted px-4 py-3 overflow-x-auto text-xs font-mono"><code>&lt;%= sui.sidebar_wrapper do |s| %&gt;</code></pre>

    <%= sui.p "Backend. Pass the stored state (:expanded or :collapsed); only a desktop toggle dispatches, never the mobile drawer or a resize:", class: "text-sm" %>
<pre class="rounded-md bg-muted px-4 py-3 overflow-x-auto text-xs font-mono"><code>&lt;%= sui.sidebar_wrapper state: current_user.sidebar_state do |s| %&gt;

shadcnrb--sidebar--component:change   detail: { state: "collapsed" }</code></pre>
  </div>

  <%= sui.separator %>

  <div class="space-y-3">
    <%= sui.h2 "The backend hook" %>
    <%= sui.p "One Stimulus controller on any ancestor catches both events, here the layout's body. This site runs exactly this, with the session as its store:", class: "text-sm" %>
<pre class="rounded-md bg-muted px-4 py-3 overflow-x-auto text-xs font-mono"><code>&lt;body data-controller="preferences"
      data-preferences-url-value="&lt;%= preferences_path %&gt;"
      data-action="shadcnrb--theme-switcher--component:change-&gt;preferences#save
                   shadcnrb--sidebar--component:change-&gt;preferences#save"&gt;</code></pre>

    <% js = <<~JS
      // app/javascript/controllers/preferences_controller.js
      import { Controller } from "@hotwired/stimulus"

      export default class extends Controller {
        static values = { url: String }

        save({ detail }) {
          fetch(this.urlValue, {
            method: "PATCH",
            headers: {
              "Content-Type": "application/json",
              "X-CSRF-Token": document.querySelector('meta[name="csrf-token"]').content
            },
            body: JSON.stringify(detail)
          })
        }
      }
    JS
    %>
    <%= sui.codeblock js, syntax: :javascript %>

    <% rb = <<~RUBY
      # config/routes.rb
      patch "preferences" => "preferences#update"

      # app/controllers/preferences_controller.rb
      class PreferencesController < ApplicationController
        def update
          current_user.update!(params.permit(:theme, :mode).merge(sidebar_state: params[:state]).compact)
          head :no_content
        end
      end
    RUBY
    %>
    <%= sui.codeblock rb %>
  </div>
</div>
